# Golden trace: OUR core (tools/linux/qca_rome_usb.c `setup`, the code the
# kext runs) uploading rampatch + NVM to the real Helios 300 BT chip 04ca:3016
# right after a cold boot (2026-11-08 00:26 IST, btusb blacklisted for that
# boot so nothing had touched the chip). Recorded independently with usbmon
# (tools/linux/usbmon_pcap.c, bus 1 dev 2) and reduced by
# tools/usbmon_reduce.py; identical line-for-line to the tool's own trace.
# Chip: rom 0x302 patch 0x111 status 0x20 -> patch 0x3e8 status 0xe0;
# 18 bulk packets; header->body gap 20.1 / 20.8 ms; body 362 ms; 384 ms total.
# Afterwards Linux btusb bound without downloading and the controller worked.
